{
  "created_at_utc": "2026-10-11T07:44:18.891864+00:00",
  "method": "Read JPEG with Pillow and convert to RGB. For analysis only, downsample keeping aspect ratio to maximum 192x192 using LANCZOS. Quantize 12 colors by deterministic median-cut with no dithering; sort by pixel count. Whole-image top 8 bins; secondary top 6 excludes nearly white pixels (minimum RGB >232) and nearly black pixels (maximum RGB <35); chromatic top 6 keeps HSV saturation >0.15 and value between 0.12 and 0.93. Fractions are within each analyzed pixel set, not full-image shares except whole palette. No source image files modified. Localized samples are per-channel median RGB values from manually named approximate normalized rectangles in the original JPEG; they expose small accents missed by area-ranked bins and may include neighboring pixels. Hue-filtered regional accents use original RGB pixels converted to HSV and documented saturation/value/hue thresholds, then median retained RGB. Their retained counts disclose how much of the region actually matches the named color.",
  "limitations": [
    "JPEG artifacts, scan color cast, aging, photograph exposure and quantization shift colors. These are approximate observed RGB values, not recovered print inks or approved brand tokens.",
    "Quantization bin counts express image area, not perceptual or semantic importance. White/black exclusions expose secondary object and accent colors but can omit dark colored regions.",
    "No historical authenticity or image provenance follows from matching pixels.",
    "Filtered accents are observed source colors, not functional UI tokens. A hue window can include similarly colored neighboring content; no contrast compliance is implied."
  ],
